t in the pipeline: Researcher: Can be used in two modes: - Greenfield: after [2C[1B[23m[22m   [2m[3mBoostrap (research the space more deeply) - Brownfield: before Scout/Plan when the task requires research (e.g., [5C[1B"how to implement X") - Also standalone: [38;5;153m/research "topic"[39m In the pipeline: Phase 1 (between Bootstrap and Scout). [1B[23m[22m [3G   [2m[3mIt takes the task → searches the web → returns structured research findings. The Planner then uses those findings [5C[1Bto build a better plan. Security: Reviews the diff specifically for security vulnerabilities: - After Review [1B[23m[22m [3G   [2m[3m(should only run if Review approved — security audit makes sense after quality gate passes) - Or in parallel with [5C[1BReview? Parallel means both get the same diff and run simultaneously. That saves time but costs more tokens. [1B[23m[22m [3G   [2m[3mSeparate phase after Review means you only audit approved code. I'll put it as a separate phase after Review (only [5C[1Bif approved). That way we don't waste tokens auditing code that hasn't passed review yet. Updated pipeline: [1B[23m[22m [3G   [38;5;153m[2m[3mBootstrap → [Research] → Scout → Plan → Code → Review → [Security] → Setup → Docs ↻ fixes[39m Now let me implement…[34C[2B[23m[22m[38;5;246mthought for 8s)[39m[K[40;1H[38;3H[?25h[?25l[H[21B[38;5;246m●[12B[38;5;174m✢[11G[38;5;216m…[23G[38;5;246m72[39m[40;1H[38;3H[?25h[?25l[H[38;5;246m  ⎿  [39mAdded[12G[1m1[14G[22mline[2C[1B   [38;5;231m[2m 19 [22m     [38;5;186m"dev-tools"[39m[K[5C[1B[38;5;231m[2m 20 [22m   ],[1B[39m [3G   [38;5;231m[2m 21 [22m   [38;5;148m"license"[38;5;231m: [38;5;186m"MIT"[38;5;231m,[1B[39m     [38;5;77m[48;5;22m 22 +[38;5;231m  [38;5;148m"author"[38;5;231m: [38;5;186m"Alexander Degtyarev <adegtyarev.ap@gmail.com>"[38;5;231m,                                           [6C[1B[49m[2m23 [22m   [38;5;148m"r