[2C[1B[39m   [38;5;231m[2m 42 [22m | `medium` | Code → Review → Setup → Docs | 6 |[5C[1B[38;5;167m[48;5;52m 41 -[38;5;231m| `complex` | Security → Code → Review → Setup → Verify → Docs | 8 |                                   [1B[49m[39m [3G   [38;5;77m[48;5;22m 43 +[38;5;231m| `complex` | Code → Review → Setup → Verify → Docs | [48;5;28m7[48;5;22m |                                              [1B[49m[39m     [38;5;231m[2m 44 [22m [12G[39m[K[5C[1B[38;5;167m[48;5;52m 43 -[38;5;231mA typo fix runs Scout, Plan, Code, Review — and stops. No environment bootstrap, no doc pass, no threat[5C[1B[38;5;167m    -[38;5;231m model. An architectural change gets all of it.                                                        [5C[1B[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 45 +[38;5;231m**Security surface** — what it exposes:                                                                [5C[1B[49m[2m 46 [22m [39m[K[5C[1B[38;5;167m[48;5;52m 45 -[38;5;231mExplore and Research run *before* Plan, so no complexity is known yet — those stay opt-in (`explore: tr[5C[1B[38;5;167m    -[38;5;231mue`, `research: true`). Any phase can be forced on or off per run or in config.                        [5C[1B[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 47 +[38;5;231m| Surface | What it means | Result |                                                                   [5C[1B[38;5;77m 48 +[38;5;231m|---------|--------------|--------|                                                                    [1B[49m[39m     [38;5;77m[48;5;22m 49 +[38;5;231m| `none` | Pure refactor, docs, tests — no attack surface | Nothing added |                            [5C[1B[38;5;77m 50 +[38;5;231m| `low` | Touches data paths, no new entry point | Planner's notes go to the Coder |                   [2C[1B[49m[39m   [38;5;77m[48;5;22m 51 +[38;5;231m| `elevated` | New input, auth, secrets, injection, dependency, or crypto surface | Dedicated Security [5C[1B[38;5;77m    +[38;5;231magent runs |                                                                                           [1B[49m[39m [3G   [38;5;231m[2m 52 [22m [39m[K[1B     [38;5;77m[48;5;22m 53 +[38;5;231mThe two are independent. A one-line change to an auth check is `trivial` + `elevated`: four agents, one[5C[1B[38;5;77m    +[38;5;231m of them Security. A large internal refactor is `complex` + `none`: seven agents, no threat model.     [5C[1B[38;5;77m 54 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                       [5C[1B[38;5;77m 55 +[38;5;231mThat split is why Security isn't just another complexity tier — risk doesn't scale with diff size. When[6C[1B[38;5;77m   +[38;5;231m the[16Grating is ambiguous, th[40G Planner is instructed to round[72Gup:[76Ga[78Gwrong[84G`elevated`[95Gcosts[101Gone[105Gagent,[112Ga[5C[1B[38;5;77m    +[38;5;231mwrong `none` ships the vulnerability.                                                                  [5C[1B[38;5;77m 56 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                       [5C[1B[38;5;77m 57 +[38;5;231mExplore and Research run *before* Plan, so no rating exists yet — those stay opt-in (`explore: true`, `[1B[49m[39m     [38;5;77m[48;5;22m    +[38;5;231mresearch: true`). Any phase can be forced on or off per run or in config.                              [5C[1B[38;5;77m 58 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                       [1B[49m[39m [3G   [38;5;231m[2m 59 [22m | Phase | Agent | What it does |[5C[1B[2m 60 [22m |-------|-------|-------------|[1B[39m [3G   [38;5;231m[2m 61 [22m | Bootstrap | bootstrapper | (Greenfield) Research similar solutions, pick stack, draft roadmap |[39m[40;1H[38;3H[?25h]0;⠂ Claude Code]0;⠐ Claude Code]0;⠂ Claude Code]0;⠐ Claude Code