[38;5;231m1. Assess task complexity (trivial/medium/complex)                                                     [5C[1B[38;5;167m 16 -[38;5;231m2. Produce an ordered list of implementation steps with files and acceptance criteria                  [5C[1B[38;5;167m 17 -[38;5;231m3. Identify risks                                                                                      [5C[1B[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 14 +[38;5;231mThe planner will:                                                                                      [5C[1B[38;5;77m 15 +[38;5;231m1. Read the parts of the codebase the task touches — call sites, tests, config                         [5C[1B[38;5;77m 16 +[38;5;231m2. Rate complexity (`trivial` / `medium` / `complex`)                                                  [5C[1B[38;5;77m 17 +[38;5;231m3. Rate the security surface (`none` / `low` / `elevated`) and flag specifics                          [5C[1B[38;5;77m 18 +[38;5;231m4. Produce ordered steps with checkable acceptance criteria                                            [5C[1B[38;5;77m 19 +[38;5;231m5. Capture a codebase context snapshot the Coder and Reviewer reuse                                    [5C[1B[49m[2m 20 [22m [39m[K[5C[1B[38;5;167m[48;5;52m 19 -[38;5;231mNote: the planner does NOT scan the repo itself — run `/ctx-scout` first, or use `/ldo` which runs both[5C[1B[38;5;167m    -[38;5;231m automatically.                                                                                        [5C[1B[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 21 +[38;5;231mIts `codebase_context` is the only repo information downstream agents get — they don't re-scan.        [6C[1B[49m[2m22[11G[22m[39m[K[5C[1B[38;5;167m[48;5;52m 21 -[38;5;231mUse before `/coder` or as the second planning stage of `/ldo`.                                         [5C[1B[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 23 +[38;5;231mUse before `/coder`, or let `/ldo` run the whole pipeline.        