true[48;5;28m "task"[48;5;22m` | Add the web research phase |                                      [5C[1B[38;5;77m 185 +[38;5;231m| `/ldo:ldo security:true [48;5;28m"task"[48;5;22m` | Force the threat model on [48;5;28m([48;5;22mor [48;5;28m`false`[48;5;22m [48;5;28mto skip it) [48;5;22m|               [5C[1B[49m[2m 186 [22m | `/ldo-bootstrap "idea"` | Start a project — prior art, stack, roadmap (interactive) |[39m[K[5C[1B[38;5;231m[2m 187 [22m | `/ldo-planner "task"` | Plan only |[39m[K[5C[1B[38;5;231m[2m 188 [22m | `/ldo-coder "task"` | Implement a plan |[39m[K[5C[1B[38;5;246m...[39m[K[5C[1B[38;5;231m[2m 191 [22m | `/ldo-researcher "topic"` | Multi-source web research |[39m[K[6C[1B[38;5;231m[2m192 [22m | `/ldo-config` | Walk through model routing |[5C[1B[2m 193 [22m | `/ldo-init` | Write the self-routing block into the project's `CLAUDE.md` |[39m[K[5C[1B[38;5;167m[48;5;52m 194 -[38;5;231m| `/ldo-agent-ux` | Shape an agent's output/context for the dual reader |                             [6C[1B[38;5;77m[48;5;22m194 +[38;5;231m| `/ldo-a[23Gnt-ux` | Write agent context and output[63Gthat a model[76Gand a[82Ghuman can both read[102G|[5C[1B[49m[2m 195 [22m [39m[K[5C[1B[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 196 +[38;5;231mWhy the punctuation differs: `/ldo:ldo` is a **workflow**, and Claude Code namespaces those by plugin.[5C[1B[38;5;77m     +[38;5;231m The `/ldo-*` commands are **skills**, which get no automatic namespace — the `ldo-` prefix is part of[5C[1B[38;5;77m     +[38;5;231m their name, so they group in the palette and don't shadow built-ins like `/init`.                    [5C[1B[38;5;77m 197 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                      [2C[1B[49m[39m   [38;5;231m[2m 198 [22m ## Use with the built-ins[5C[1B[2m 199 [22m [1B[39m [3G   [38;5;231m[2m 200 [22m LDO deliberately doesn't re