;5;231mnents in a layout Claude Code couldn't find, so the plugin installed empty. `/plugin update ldo@ldo-ai[5C[1B[38;5;77m     +[38;5;231m` fixes it.                                                                                           [5C[1B[38;5;77m 294 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                      [5C[1B[38;5;77m 295 +[38;5;231m**"Update now" is greyed out, with "Local plugins cannot be updated remotely."** Installs from before [5C[1B[38;5;77m     +[38;5;231mv1.3.1 were registered as a local source. Reinstall once to switch to the git source:                 [7C[1B[38;5;77m96 +[38;5;231m   [16G        [25G     [31G    [36G      [43G    [48G     [54G      [61G      [68G       [76G    [81G  [84G   [88G [90G    [95G [97G    [102G   [106G        [6C[1B[38;5;77m297 +[38;5;231m```                                                [64G       [72G    [77G    [82G        [91G      [98G            [5C[1B[38;5;77m 298 +[38;5;231m/plugin uninstall ldo@ldo-ai                                                                          [5C[1B[38;5;77m 299 +[38;5;231m/plugin marketplace update ldo-ai                                                                     [5C[1B[38;5;77m 300 +[38;5;231m/plugin install ldo@ldo-ai                                                                            [5C[1B[38;5;77m 301 +[38;5;231m```                                                                                                   [5C[1B[38;5;77m 302 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                      [5C[1B[38;5;77m 303 +[38;5;231m**Routing changes aren't taking effect.** You probably created `ldo-config.json`. Nothing reads it — s[5C[1B[38;5;77m     +[38;5;231mee [[38;5;186mConfiguration[38;5;231m](#configuration). Put the routing in `CLAUDE.md` or ask for it in th