8;5;231mection keeps describing a phase removed three changes ago. A term is used in one place and defined in [5C[1B[38;5;77m     +[38;5;231manother that was later cut.                                                                           [1B[49m[39m [3G   [38;5;77m[48;5;22m 151 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                      [1B[49m[39m     [38;5;77m[48;5;22m 152 +[38;5;231mFor that, `/ldo-docs-audit` reads everything cold — deliberately before looking at the source, so gaps[5C[1B[38;5;77m     +[38;5;231m aren't filled from memory — and reports contradictions, stale claims, undefined jargon, and the worst[5C[1B[38;5;77m     +[38;5;231m category: instructions that quietly do nothing, where the reader believes they configured something a[5C[1B[38;5;77m     +[38;5;231mnd nothing errors.                                                                                    [8C[1B[38;5;77m3[12G[38;5;231m [14G                 [32G [34G    [39G   [43G    [48G    [53G   [57G    [62G      [69G       [77G [5C[1B[38;5;77m 154 +[38;5;231mIf you ran `/ldo-init`, the Coder appends a line to a drift log in `CLAUDE.md` after each user-facing [5C[1B[38;5;77m     +[38;5;231mchange. Around eight entries, Claude offers the audit. It offers rather than runs — a full read costs [5C[1B[38;5;77m     +[38;5;231mreal tokens, and the timing is yours.                                                                 [5C[1B[38;5;77m 155 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                      [2C[1B[49m[39m   [38;5;231m[2m 156 [22m ## Usage[39m[K[5C[1B[38;5;231m[2m 157 [22m [1B[39m [3G   [38;5;231m[2m 158 [22m Type `ldo` in the command palette and everything clusters together.[17C[2B[38;5;246m6[39m[40;1H[35;3H[?25h[?25l[H[K[8C[1B[38;5;231m[2m2[12G[22m**Review finds 