e" is a do[31Gumented complaint, not a[56Gnitpick.     [70G        [79G      [86G           [98G   [102G      [109G     [5C[1B[49m[2m 25 [22m - `?` shows help, `/` searches, `:` opens a command line if you have one.[39m[K[5C[1B[38;5;167m[48;5;52m 26 -[38;5;231m- `j`/`k` or arrows scroll; `g`/`G` top and bottom; `Tab` moves focus; `Enter` selects.                [5C[1B[38;5;77m[48;5;22m 26 +[38;5;231m- `j`/`k` or arrows scroll; `g`/`G` top and bottom; `Tab` moves focus; `Enter` [48;5;28mconfirms, `Space` toggle[5C[1B[38;5;77m[48;5;22m    +[38;5;231m[48;5;28ms[48;5;22m.                                                                                                     [5C[1B[49m[2m 27 [22m [39m[K[5C[1B[38;5;231m[2m 28 [22m Show the keybindings on screen, at least until the user is fluent. `?` is expected; a hidden keymap is [6C[1B[2m  [11G[22ma dead end.[7C[1B[2m9[11G[22m[39m[K[5C[1B[K[1B[38;5;231m●[3G[39mТеперь добавляю[19Gплотную[27Gсекцию[34Gпро[38Gловушки[46Gкодирования[58Gклавиш[65G—[67Gэто[71Gто,[75Gчего[80Gреально[88Gне[91Gхватало.[2B[38;5;246m●[3G[39m[1mUpdate[22m(skills/ldo-tui/SKILL.md)[K[16C[2B[38;5;246m9[39m[40;1H[34;3H[?25h[?25l[H[11C[29B[38;5;174mg…[102C[2B[38;5;246m100% context used[39m[40;1H[34;3H[?25h[?25l[H[29B[38;5;174m·[3G[38;5;180mCogitating…[39m[40;1H[34;3H[?25h[?25l[H[6G[38;5;77m[48;5;22m    +[38;5;231myou will hit this — so design for the lowest common denominator, not the terminal you're testing in.   [1B[49m[39m [3G [5G [38;5;77m[48;5;22m 66 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                       [49m[39m[K[2C[1B   [38;5;77m[48;5;22m 67 +[38;5;231m- **`Ctrl` + letter is `key & 0x1F`.** So `Ctrl-M` is Enter, `Ctrl-I` is Tab, `Ctrl-H` is Backspace, `C[49m[39m[K[2C[1B   [38;5;77m[48;5;22m    +[38;5;231mtrl-[` is Esc, `Ctrl-D` is end-of-file. You can't bind these as distinct actions.                      [49m[39m[K[2C[1B   [38;5;77m[48;5;22m 68 +[38;5;231m- **`Ctrl-S` / `Ctrl-Q` are XON/XOFF.** With default TTY settings the kernel freezes output on `Ctrl-S`[49m[39m[K[2C[1B   [38;5;77m[48;5;22m    +[38;5;231m and your app never sees the key — the screen just stops. Don't bind them; if you must, tell users to `[5C[1B[38;5;77m    +[38;5;231mstty -ixon`.                                                                                           [1B[49m[39m [3G   [38;5;77m[48;5;22m 69 +[38;5;231m- **`Ctrl+Shift+letter` is indistinguishable from `Ctrl+letter`** in the legacy encoding. Shift as a se[1B[49m[39m     [38;5;77m[48;5;22m    +[38;5;231mparate modifier needs the Kitty protocol, below.                                                       [5C[1B[38;5;77m 70 +[38;5;231m- **macOS has no Meta key by default.** Option composes characters; `Alt`/`Meta` bindings silently do n[5C[1B[38;5;77m    +[38;5;231mothing until the user changes a terminal setting. Never make a Meta binding essential.                 [5C[1B[38;5;77m 71 +[38;5;231m- **Modifier + arrow is unreliable** — encodings vary across terminals and terminfo has no standard cap[5C[1B[38;5;77m    +[38;5;231ms for `Ctrl`/`Alt`+arrow. Bare arrows are safe; modified arrows aren't.                                [6C[1B[38;5;77m72[13G[38;5;231m**[16GEsc` is[24Gambiguous.** The[41Gbyte[46G`0x1B` is[56Gboth a[63Glone Esc and the prefix of every escape sequence, [10C[1Bo[13Gpa[16Gsers wait on a t[33Gmer to decide — and under[59G`tmux` tha[70G timer defaults to half[94Ga sec[100Gnd. A l[108Gggy E[10C[1Bc[13Gis[16Ga terminal pr[30Gblem, not yours, but i[53G's[56Gwhy Esc-to-quit[72Gcan[76Gfeel[81Gsluggish.[5C[1B[38;5;77m 73 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                       [5C[1B[38;5;77m 74 +[38;5;231mThe **Kitty keyboard protocol** (`CSI u`) fixes the ambiguity and is supported by kitty, foot, Ghostty,[6C[1B[38;5;77m  [11G[38;5;231m iTerm2, WezTe[26Gm, Ala[34Gitty, Windows Terminal, and the libraries Textual (≥0.67), Bubble Tea v2, and cr[10C[1Bossterm.[20G**But[26G`tmux`[33Gdoes[38Gnot[42Gpass[47Git[50Gthrough**[60G—[62Gthe[66Genable[73Gsequence[82Gis[85Gsilently[94Gdropped,[103Gand[107Ga[109Glarge[5C[1B[38;5;77m    +[38;5;231m share of users run inside a multiplexer. Design for the legacy encoding; opt into Kitty as progressive[5C[1B[38;5;77m    +[38;5;231m enhancement when you detect it.                                                                       [5C[1B[38;5;77m 75 +[38;5;231m                                                                                                       [6C[1B[49m[2m76[11G[22m## Process — two passes, with a critique between[5C[1B[2m 77 [22m [1B[39m [3G   [38;5;231m[2m 78 [22m **Pass 1: design before code.** Decide stream vs. full-screen. Sketch the layout in ASCII and write out[5C[1B[2m    [22m  the keymap and the palette — three colours at most, each with a job. Write the one sentence a first-ti[1B[39m [3G   [38;5;231m[2m    [22m me user reads on launch.[39m[40;1H[34;3H[?25h[?25l[H[2C[29B[38;5;216mCogitating…[39m[40;1H[34;3H[?25h]0;⠂ Claude Code]0;⠐ Claude Code[?25l[H[6G[K[7C[1B[38;5;77m[48;5;22m7[11G[38;5;231m-[13G**`Ctrl`[22G+[24Gletter[31Gis[34G`key[39G&[41G0x1F`.**[50GSo[53G`Ctrl-M`[62Gis[65GEnter,[72G`Ctrl-I`[81Gis[84GTab,[89G`Ctrl-H`[98Gis[101GBackspace,[112G`C[6C[1B[38;5;77m  [11G[38;5;231mtrl-[` is Esc, `Ct[30Gl-D` is end-of-file. You can't b[63Gnd th[69Gse[72Gas distinct[84Gactions.     [98G  [101G          [112G  [6C[1B[38;5;77m68[11G[38;5;231m- **`Ctrl-S` /[32GQ[35Gare XON/XOFF.**[51GWith default TTY settings the kernel freezes[96Goutput[103Gon[106G`Ctrl-