[2C[1B[23m[22m [5G [2m[3mthem. The challenge: I'm an agent in a Claude Code session. Can I invoke the workflow? The workflow [38;5;153mldo.js[39m lives [2C[1B[23m[22m   [2m[3min [38;5;153mworkflows/ldo.js[39m in this project. But the workflow runtime is invoked via the Workflow tool. However, I'm [23m[22m[K[2C[1B   [2m[3mcurrently running as a background subagent (the channel-dev-lead orchestrator), and the Workflow tool may or may [5C[1Bnot be available to me. Let me check what I actually have. My tool list includes the Workflow tool. Let me look... [2C[1B[23m[22m   [2m[3mActually, the Workflow tool IS in my available tools (it's listed in the function list at the top: "Workflow"). But[5C[1Bthere's a constraint: "ONLY call this tool when the user has explicitly opted into multi-agent orchestration." The[1B[23m[22m [3G   [2m[3muser just said "сделай сам" — do it yourself — which is an explicit instruction to run the pipeline. That's opt-in[5C[1Benough. But wait — the bigger problem. The workflow calls [38;5;153magent(prompt, {agentType: 'planner', ...})[39m. For those [1B[23m[22m [3G   [2m[3magent types to resolve, the agents need to be registered. In THIS session, the agents are at [38;5;153magents/[39m (plugin-roo…[2B[23m[22m[38;5;174m✻[3GMetamorphosing… [29G[38;5;246mthought for 83s)[39m[K[10C[1B[38;5;246mUse[15G/btw to ask[27Ga quick[35Gside question[49Gwithout[57Ginterrupting Claude's current work[39m[K[5C[1B[K[102C[1B[K[40;1H[34;3H[?25h[?25l[H[3Gфайлов,[11Gтипы[16G[38;5;153mplanner[39m/[38;5;153mcoder[39m/[38;5;153mreviewer[39G[39m[1mпропали[47G[22mиз[50Gдоступных[60G—[62Gпрямое[69Gсвидетельство,[84Gчто[88Gголые[94Gимена[100Gне[103Gрезолвятся.[115GЕсли[2C[1Bпри установленно[20G плагине[29Gто же самое — сломае[50Gся каждый вызов агента, то[77Gесть[82Gвесь[87Gпайплайн.[97GЭто[101Gне[104Gподтверждено[117Gи[2C[1Bпотенциально фа[19G